#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# adjugate

#% text
# `adjugate(m)` gives the adjugate of the square matrix `m`: the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `m . adjugate(m)` equals `det(m)` times the identity matrix, also when `m` is singular.

#% item
# The entry `[i, j]` is `(-1)^(i + j)` times the determinant of `m` without row `j` and column `i`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
adjugate([[5, 4], [4, 11]])
#% output
#= [[11, -4], [-4, 5]]

#% cell
adjugate([[a, b], [c, d]])
#% output
#= [[d, -b], [-c, a]]

#% cell
adjugate([[15, 3, 4], [3, 15, 11], [-2, 1, 7]])
#% output
#= [[94, -17, -27], [-43, 113, -153], [33, -21, 216]]

#% text
# The defining identity:

#% cell
dot(adjugate([[15, 3, 4], [3, 15, 11], [-2, 1, 7]]), [[15, 3, 4], [3, 15, 11], [-2, 1, 7]]) == det([[15, 3, 4], [3, 15, 11], [-2, 1, 7]])*identity_matrix(3)
#% output
#= true

